From 48041fc65a4f1ee8f663459fc5dd5395b2e84e48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:54:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] Claude Code plugin: install and repair the hooks

konsole-claude-setup adds the hooks that drive the plugin to Claude
Code's settings ($CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json, by default
~/.claude/settings.json), or removes them, or says whether they are
there. It only ever touches hooks that run claude-code-hook, replaces a
hook at an old path instead of adding a second, backs the file up before
a change and refuses to touch one that is not valid JSON.

The plugin offers Install and Uninstall Claude Code Hooks in its menu,
and the Claude Sessions panel shows a banner with an Install button while
they are missing. It watches the settings, so the banner follows changes
made anywhere, including Claude Code dropping the hooks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
